Let $\lambda\in \mathbb C\setminus \sigma(-\Delta_\xi)$. We define the Green function associated with the fiber operator $-\Delta_\xi$ by
\begin{equation}\label{equ:Gfourier}
G_\lambda^\xi(x,y)
:=
\sum_{k\in\Lambda^*}
\frac{e_k(x)\overline{e_k(y)}}{|k+\xi|^2-\lambda}
=
\frac{1}{|Y|}\sum_{k\in\Lambda^*}
\frac{e^{i(k+\xi)\cdot (x-y)}}{|k+\xi|^2-\lambda}
,
\qquad x,y\in Y.
\end{equation}
The series is understood in \(L^2(Y\times Y)\), as justified in
Proposition~\ref{prop:resolvent_kernel}.

\label{coro:refined-K-double}
Under the assumptions of Proposition~\ref{prop:general-xi-effective},
with \(K\in\Xi\), the two characteristic values coincide at \(\xi=K\).  Their common
value satisfies
\begin{equation}\label{equ:lambda0-refined-K}
\widehat\lambda_0^\epsilon(\eta)
=
\frac{2\pi}{|D|\eta^2L}
\left[
1-\frac{2\pi\kappa_K}{|D|L}
+
O\left(
\frac1{L^2}
+\frac{\epsilon}{\eta^2L^2}
\right)
\right],
\end{equation}
where \(\kappa_K\) is defined by \eqref{equ:kappa-xi} at \(\xi=K\).
Its geometric multiplicity is two.

\label{rem:exact-Dirac-cone}
The uniform eigenvalue error in Theorem~\ref{thm:refined-Dirac-point}
does not by itself prove a nonzero conical slope.  Instead, differentiating
the exact operator pencil and taking its Schur complement on the
two-dimensional kernel proves that the exact off-diagonal
first-order coefficient is nonzero; see
Appendix~\ref{app:exact-Dirac-cone}.
Under the same hypotheses, for sufficiently small \(\eta\) and
\(\epsilon/(\eta^2L)\), the two exact characteristic values satisfy
\begin{align}
 \widehat\lambda_\pm(K+h)
 ={}&\widehat\lambda_0^\epsilon(\eta)
 \pm\left[
 \frac{4\pi^2|c|}{|D|\eta^2L^2}
 +O\left(\frac1{\eta^2L^3}
          +\frac{\epsilon}{\eta^4L^3}\right)
 \right]|h|+O_{\epsilon,\eta}(|h|^2),\qquad h\to0.
 \label{equ:exact-Dirac-cone}
\end{align}
The slope is strictly positive.
